2.0.0-rc.31 — the Library grows three voices: the VESSEL (a bowed bell that goes on ringing after the bow lifts — the reverie's own instrument), the REGAL (a small reed organ in the second chapter and the seizure, and now and then it takes a cadence off the hummers) and the FLUE (a recorder, the rarest speaker in the room); the music box is DAMPED now, its old open sound retired; the lute stop, the cello's harmonics and three drone registrations sit on the desk as knobs; every scene rests somebody, so the chapters finally sound different from each other; and every evening after the first announces its cast in the log ("tonight: harpsichord, lute stop · music box, damped · drone, principal · the vessel back…")
